cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Marine metallothionein structure encodes environmental
  niche: code and data
message: >-
  If you use this software or data, please cite it using the
  metadata below. A manuscript reporting these results is in
  preparation, and this entry will be updated when it is
  available.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rochlani
    given-names: Vivaan
repository-code: https://github.com/vivs999/marine-mt-structure
abstract: >-
  Code and processed data for a study of whether the structure
  of marine metallothionein proteins carries a recoverable
  signal of the environment that the organism lives in.
  Zn(2+)-bound structures were predicted with Boltz-1 for 535
  sequences from 272 marine species. Random Forest models
  trained on Zn(2+) coordination geometry and ESM-2 embeddings
  classified habitat with 88.9 percent accuracy on held-out
  species, and predicted sea surface temperature at Pearson r
  of 0.665. No signal was recovered for salinity, pH, or
  depth.
keywords:
  - metallothionein
  - marine biology
  - protein structure prediction
  - machine learning
  - Boltz-1
  - ESM-2
  - environmental adaptation
